<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ian Smith</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1919–2007</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ian Smith was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodesian-front">Rhodesian Front</a> politician who became prime minister of Southern Rhodesia in 1964. On 11 November 1965 his government issued the Unilateral Declaration of Independence to avoid majority rule, creating the unrecognised state of Rhodesia. After a long <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war he agreed the Internal Settlement of 1978, which produced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a> Rhodesia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ian-smith.jpg" alt="Ian Smith" width="250" height="341" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Colin Weyer, photographer · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ian_Smith_1975.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
